# AGENTS.md

## Purpose

This repository follows an opinionated Python/Nuxt golden path. Keep changes small, documented, tested, and tied to the active project task.

## Required Start

Run or read project status first:

```bash
make project-status
```

Then load:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `project/state.yaml`
- `project/index.md`
- the active task from `project/tasks/`

Then use `.agents/context-map.yaml` to load only task-relevant context.

## Architecture Rules

- Start from the current project type: `{{ project_type }}`.
- Start from the current runtime level: `{{ runtime_level }}`.
- Do not add databases, queues, caches, external services, authentication, Kubernetes, or production deployment unless a requirement, ADR, and approval level justify it.
- Backend business logic belongs outside FastAPI routes.
- Backend domain code must not import FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, or infrastructure clients.
- Frontend pages compose features; feature logic belongs in feature composables or services.
- API types must be generated from OpenAPI once a backend API contract exists.

## Standard Commands

```bash
make setup
make dev
make test
make lint
make typecheck
make check
make project-status
make sync-project-docs
make validate-project
make task-ready TASK=T-001
make task-start TASK=T-001
make task-review TASK=T-001
make task-complete TASK=T-001
make task-block TASK=T-001 REASON="..." UNBLOCK="..."
```

## Approval Boundaries

- A0: small fixes, tests, documentation, local refactors, next-task proposals.
- A1: public behavior changes, new endpoints, new modules, non-destructive schema changes.
- A2: scope changes, production deployment, destructive data changes, auth changes, new infrastructure services, paid external services, project retirement.
- `make task-approve` is for humans only. AI agents must not autonomously record A1 or A2 approval.

## Workflow

Use `docs/workflow.md` for the daily change loop and `.agents/skills/` for task-specific procedures. Do not bypass controlled task transitions by silently editing task status. After task or project state changes, run `make sync-project-docs` when dashboards need refresh and then `make validate-project`.
